Subject: [PATCH] toolkit: load the Aequera in-content layer from common-shared.css

Why Firefox source must change:
  Firefox's in-content pages (Settings, Add-ons, the network and
  certificate error pages, about:config, about:support, about:protections,
  dialogs) take their look from design tokens that
  toolkit/themes/shared/in-content/common-shared.css imports. Settings and
  the new error card are built from shadow-DOM components, so a page
  stylesheet cannot restyle them, and no pref, policy, or theme can add a
  stylesheet to every in-content page. One import in the shared sheet does,
  and it reaches the shadow roots that link a sheet importing it.

What it changes (one @import, after Firefox's token imports):
  chrome://global/skin/in-content/aequera-in-content.css, a toolkit-
  namespace URL that toolkit itself does not ship: the overlay
  "shell-chrome" points it at its stylesheet with a chrome override
  (jar.mn), so toolkit names no browser file and depends on nothing in
  browser/. Without the override the import loads nothing. The stylesheet
  redefines Firefox's tokens (accent, surfaces, text, borders, radii)
  from aequera/design/tokens.toml; every rule sits inside
  @media -moz-pref("aequera.incontent.enabled") and steps aside under
  prefers-contrast and forced colors. No markup, string, or behavior
  changes.

Depends on: overlay "shell-chrome" (the override, the stylesheet, and the
  token sheet it imports).
Validation: aequera/shell/firefox/tests/browser/browser_aequera_incontent.js
  (Settings, Add-ons, and an error page take the Aequera accent and
  canvas; the error card's shadow root shows the Aequera illustration;
  pref off and forced colors restore Firefox's tokens; about:privatebrowsing
  keeps its own design); Firefox's in-content tests with the pref off.
Upstream risk: low for the patch (one line next to two stable imports).
  The stylesheet names Firefox's token variables; a renamed token falls
  back to Firefox's value (a cosmetic regression, never a broken page),
  and the test checks the main ones.

diff --git a/toolkit/themes/shared/in-content/common-shared.css b/toolkit/themes/shared/in-content/common-shared.css
index 84cba8cfb76a..564f2661c7e2 100644
--- a/toolkit/themes/shared/in-content/common-shared.css
+++ b/toolkit/themes/shared/in-content/common-shared.css
@@ -4,6 +4,9 @@
 
 @import url("chrome://global/skin/design-system/tokens-brand.css");
 @import url("chrome://global/skin/design-system/text-and-typography.css");
+/* Aequera in-content layer: the product supplies this URL (a chrome
+ * override); nothing is loaded without one. */
+@import url("chrome://global/skin/in-content/aequera-in-content.css");

 @namespace html "http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml";
 @namespace xul "http://www.mozilla.org/keymaster/gatekeeper/there.is.only.xul";
